## /a step back
I am posting something here after a whole while - sorry for that. It is just like with learning. If you do not establish a routine
of regularly doing/revising something then it gets forgotten quite fast. Or even if it does not get forgotten as in the case 
of my own blog - there simply is not enough time to sit down and start typing on this. <br>
And this is a fairly normal process in general. Establishing routines however is a hard thing itself. You do need to keep it going
because usually it is way easier to loose the routines than to gradually build them. <br>
And another remark that recently came to my mind: Routines do define who you are. <br>
Even if might go unnoticed by others these routines define who you are in a very specific way and moment. 

## /Learning is hard
Just like you have to "learn" your routines I think it is quite fascinating to think about learning in a similar way.
I sadly do not remember where I stumbled upon this in my way around content on the internet but it stuck to me. <br>
Learning is equal to changing the person you are <br>
If you learn something you inherently have to struggle. Just like the caterpillar that has to get out of its cocoon 
after its metamorphosis. You struggle, your learn, you change. <br>

## /Change - a doule-edged sword?
And in some way I do believe that change can be somewhat of a double-edged sword. I mean personally I really like the Idea
of change. I am curious and love to learn new things. I do think that is partly why I took the route into CS. <br>
However I think it is in some sense natural for humans to despice change if the situation they are currently in is just
good enough. <br>
This is why change - and learning as well - is something that is just naturally hard to archieve. You just have to go 
through a phase of "this feels bad" to evolve and learn and change at the end of the day. <br>
And I believe this is why this thought was burned into my brain the last few weeks since i've heard it. And which is probably why I 
just had to share this.
<br>
<br>
Stuggle, Learn, Change. <br>
Greetings - Johannes